          "Alma: Most founders who write to us from Spain or elsewhere in Europe assume manufacturing in India begins by emailing a finished tech pack into an anonymous inbox and waiting for a quote. We work differently. Anyone commissioning work through KarmaRise meets the exact people responsible for their order. We have face and eyes. We show them from day one.",
          "I travel back and forth between Spain and India every few months and carry out fieldwork before, during, and after each order, though I am usually the first person you speak with from Europe. My first step is a live video call. Face to face, you catch details an email chain misses: a brief pause over a lining weight, or the exact gesture a boutique owner makes when describing how a leather bag should feel as a shopper lifts it off a shelf. Instead of a machine behind a screen firing back stock questions, you get a two-way conversation on [how we coordinate production between Spain and India](/how-we-work).",
          "On that first call, I let the Client speak freely. Nine times out of ten, I still offer small prompts to help sort out what they want. Someone who lifts the shutter of their shop every morning may never have produced a handbag or a cotton or linen garment, yet they know down to the stitch what their shoppers expect. I take notes on every point as we talk, just as I did in my previous companies, and I never wait for the other side to send a recap. Straight after we hang up, I email back our written call conclusions point by point and ask for written confirmation. Everybody forgets what they said. Me first. Once every agreement sits on paper, both sides read from the same page.",
