          "Across our calls, three clear situations come up. First come founders who ran own-brand lines before COVID, paused or closed when the shock hit retail hard, and still carry some caution about starting again, even as that fear slowly fades and their trade instinct stays sharp. Next come brands already producing in India or abroad who want direct communication and stricter quality checks. Then come first-time founders with a strong eye for their own window display who need straight guidance from minute one.",
          "There is another hesitation several people share in a lower voice, even though it makes me uncomfortable to hear it: distrust of India. I understand where it comes from. Years ago, working on the European side helping international Clients import from China, China was just opening to global trade and starting to manufacture everything. Early importers got burnt often back then, until China built its standing and could no longer afford to fail Europe. Many shops in Spain still lack that direct track record with India, so one delay or bad story gets pinned on the whole country. Add the weight of a first order on top of that. You can talk with me ten times over ten months and still stay tense until the first carton lands, because plenty of people say yes to everything and vanish when delivery comes due. That is why I never make easy promises. Weather, freight, or a dye batch can nudge a date because they sit outside my control. What does stay in our hands is checking every stage two, three, five times over. And I give my life before I fail a Client.",
